App class
Untested main class of the program (Shows the overall structure of the WaterTrackerAPP)

WaterUsageRecord class:
Defines the WaterUsageRecord Object and its Constructor that is used to record water usage

The object has attributes of:
(WaterFixture fixture, LocalDate date, double litres)
// LocalDate Object String like "2026-11-13" in "format (YYYY-MM-DD)"
This mainly serves as a blueprint for record objects

Methods:
getFixture() - returns the stored WaterFixture object
setFixture(WaterFixture newFixture) - used in constructor to set WaterFixture object
getDate() - returns LocalDate object
setDate(LocalDate newDate) - used in constructor to set the usage date
getLitres() - returns litres of water used as double 
setLitres(Double newLitres) - used in constructor to set the usage amount

Household class:

attributes:
ArrayList<WaterFixture> fixtures :
This is an arraylist used to store created WaterFixture objects

ArrayList<WaterUsageRecord> records
This is an arraylist used to store created WaterUsageRecord objects
    // format records[ WaterUsageRecord obj1(WaterFixture obj, LocalDate obj, double litres),Record2(WaterFixture obj, LocalDate obj, double litres) ]
    // format WaterFixture obj( String givenName, double givenWFR from subclass)

Methods:
getFixtureArrayList() - Returns an arraylist of fixtures objects
getRecordArrayList() -  Returns an arraylist of record objects
addFixture(WaterFixture fixture) - adds a fixture object to the Fixture arraylist
recordUsage(WaterFixture fixture, LocalDate date, double amount) - adds a record object to the record arraylist
displayRecords(ArrayList<WaterUsageRecord> recordArrayList) - prints out the stored record list
displayFixtures(ArrayList<WaterFixture> fixtureArrayList) -prints out the stored fixture list